  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_10. Let triangle MNO be a triangle with sides MN = 10, NO = 14, where \u2220N = 48\u00b0. Let triangle RST be a triangle with sides RS = 15, ST = 21, where \u2220S = 48\u00b0. Triangle MNO is similar to triangle RST by SAS similarity with scale factor 1.5 (congruent angle pairs: N \u2245 S). Find the measure of \u2220T in RST.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A designer is comparing two triangular components for a mechanical system. The first triangle MNO has sides MN = 10 and NO = 14, with an angle of 48\u00b0 at vertex N. The second triangle RST has sides RS = 15 and ST = 21, with an angle of 48\u00b0 at vertex S.\n\nThe designer notices that the two triangles are similar by the Side-Angle-Side Similarity Theorem, with a scale factor of 1.5 (the angle at N is congruent to the angle at S).\n\nSince the triangles are similar with this correspondence, what is the measure of angle T in triangle RST?"
